sys.setrecursionlimit(10000000)
#for 7.2, this code is going to use the coordinate list from 7.1 to determine the splitters that are not used, and then replace
#all unused splitters with dots. After the data has been cleaned, a recursive algorithm will systematically determine the 
#unique number of pathways a beam of light can take in the cleaned input by giving values to each splitter from the bottem
#up in a left to right pattern. These values will represent the corresponding quantity of unique pathways a beam will take 
#if it hits the splitter. Splitters higher up in the chain will represent the sum of lower splitters. This will be done through
#a coordinate plane input that has been cleaned, and the splitter value data will be stored in a corresponding and similar 
#array of coordinates. 

